{
  "id": "m22l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Métodos y campos mutables",
    "en": "Methods and mutable fields"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Más que datos"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una dataclass puede tener **métodos** normales que usan sus campos."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from dataclasses import dataclass",
          "",
          "@dataclass",
          "class Rectangulo:",
          "    ancho: float",
          "    alto: float",
          "    def area(self):",
          "        return self.ancho * self.alto",
          "",
          "print(Rectangulo(2, 3).area())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Para un campo **mutable** (lista, dict) NO uses `[]` como valor por defecto: usa `field(default_factory=list)`, que crea una lista nueva para cada objeto."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from dataclasses import dataclass, field",
          "",
          "@dataclass",
          "class Cesta:",
          "    items: list = field(default_factory=list)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Compartir una lista por defecto entre objetos es un error clásico; default_factory lo evita."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "More than data"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A dataclass can have normal **methods** that use its fields."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from dataclasses import dataclass",
          "",
          "@dataclass",
          "class Rectangulo:",
          "    ancho: float",
          "    alto: float",
          "    def area(self):",
          "        return self.ancho * self.alto",
          "",
          "print(Rectangulo(2, 3).area())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "For a **mutable** field (list, dict) do NOT use `[]` as default: use `field(default_factory=list)`, which creates a fresh list for each object."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from dataclasses import dataclass, field",
          "",
          "@dataclass",
          "class Cesta:",
          "    items: list = field(default_factory=list)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Sharing one default list across objects is a classic bug; default_factory prevents it."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m22l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define una dataclass `Rectangulo` con `ancho` y `alto`, y un método `area()` que devuelva su producto.",
        "en": "Define a dataclass `Rectangulo` with `ancho` and `alto`, and an `area()` method returning their product."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass",
        "",
        "# completa la dataclass con el método area()"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass",
        "",
        "@dataclass",
        "class Rectangulo:",
        "    ancho: float",
        "    alto: float",
        "    def area(self):",
        "        return self.ancho * self.alto"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "El método usa self.ancho y self.alto."
        ],
        "en": [
          "The method uses self.ancho and self.alto."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "Rectangulo",
          "harness": "assert Rectangulo(2, 3).area() == 6\nassert Rectangulo(5, 4).area() == 20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m22l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define una dataclass `Cesta` con `items` (lista por defecto vacía con default_factory) y un método `add(x)` que lo añada.",
        "en": "Define a dataclass `Cesta` with `items` (empty list default via default_factory) and an `add(x)` method that appends it."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass, field",
        "",
        "# completa la dataclass con add(x)"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass, field",
        "",
        "@dataclass",
        "class Cesta:",
        "    items: list = field(default_factory=list)",
        "    def add(self, x):",
        "        self.items.append(x)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "items: list = field(default_factory=list).",
          "add hace self.items.append(x)."
        ],
        "en": [
          "items: list = field(default_factory=list).",
          "add does self.items.append(x)."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "Cesta",
          "harness": "c = Cesta()\nc.add('a'); c.add('b')\nassert c.items == ['a', 'b']\nassert Cesta().items == []"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}